Round 76 - post-fix leak verification (no new findings requested)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
An independent post-fix leak sweep found one remaining surface: the
linter printed an env-equal deprecated reason (`L005 ... use
Zx9... instead`) because the linter is hermetic and built its redactor
without the process environment. The CLI now sweeps every lint
finding message with the analyzed material profile before reporting in
text, JSON, and SARIF; the benign-prose control stays readable.

Round 76 verified: the raw value appears in none of the three formats,
`L005` and `***SECRET***` do, the regression test drives the real
binary, and JSON/SARIF shapes stay valid.

VERDICT: LINT-LEAK FIXED.

